## Interpretation

- If the trained probe becomes accurate earlier than the logit lens, the next number is linearly represented before Qwen's native unembedding is aligned to decode it.
- If both curves rise together, the information becomes available and natively readable at approximately the same depth.
- If only the final layers become accurate, Qwen may compute the answer late rather than carrying a stable early representation.
- A large train–test gap means the probe is memorizing generation-specific structure; the held-out-seed curve is the relevant result.

The comparison is deliberately numeric-vocabulary-restricted. A full-vocabulary logit lens answers a different question because punctuation, whitespace, and nonnumeric tokens compete with the target.